    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d304">

                <pb facs="0254" n="204" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg204"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/208</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the Advisory Commission of Railway
                        Experts to Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stevens</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1917-11-04T04:30:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1917-11-03T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            November 4, 1917, 4.30 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For Willard:</p>
                <p>I am leaving Petrograd to try to improve operation of lines Omsk to Moscow to
                    handle vast amount of food Siberia to Central Russia. Russian Government claims
                    this is the most important problem in Russia and absolutely vital to existence.
                    Can you send eight more <pb facs="0255" n="205" xml:id="pg205"/> units if I find
                    necessary? Have gratifying reports from Siberian line.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stevens</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
